      summary:
        '<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/af/a0/afa04ee3-414f-4481-8d23-7e7c146f192e/content/images/2026/07/patch_tuesday.png" alt="Microsoft Patch Tuesday for July 2026 &#x2014; Snort rules and prominent vulnerabilities"><p>Microsoft has released its monthly security update for July 2026, which includes 622 vulnerabilities affecting a range of products, including 57 that Microsoft marked as &quot;critical.&quot;</p><p>Microsoft notes that two of the vulnerabilities disclosed this month have been exploited in the wild.</p><p><a href="https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-56155">CVE-2026-56155</a> is an important-severity elevation of privilege vulnerability in Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS) caused by insufficient granularity of access control. An authorized attacker could use it to elevate privileges locally.</p><p><a href="https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-56164">CVE-2026-56164</a> is a moderate-severity vulnerability in M',
