      hash: "c0cacd6c8edbf0d33c3b7788a07d0a66babbfe8783458d0709bae3547470c0a0",
      summary:
        '<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/af/a0/afa04ee3-414f-4481-8d23-7e7c146f192e/content/images/2026/06/threat_source-3.jpg" alt="Catan and Mouse"><p>Welcome to this week&#x2019;s edition of the Threat Source newsletter.&#xA0;&#xA0;</p><blockquote><em>&#x201C;I do not know everything; still many things I understand.&#x201D; </em><br>&#x2015; Madeleine L&apos;Engle, A Wrinkle in Time&#xA0;</blockquote><blockquote><em>&#x201C;Don&apos;t try to&#xA0;comprehend with&#xA0;your mind. Your&#xA0;minds are&#xA0;very limited. Use your intuition.&#x201D; </em><br>&#x2015; Madeleine L&apos;Engle, A Wind in the Door&#xA0;</blockquote><p>The World Cup. The 4<sup>th</sup>&#xA0;of July as&#xA0;the US turns 250. Dungeon Crawler Carl.&#xA0;LeBron&#xA0;moving&#xA0;on. Wimbledon. AI.&#xA0;There&#xA0;are&#xA0;so many things that I could draw&#xA0;a parallel&#xA0;to&#xA0;farm&#xA0;for this week&#x2019;s newsletter&#xA0;content.&#xA0;So&#xA0;let&#x2019;s&#xA0;talk about board games.&#xA0;&#xA0;<br>&#xA0;<br>A',
